---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "kotoba-lang EDA";
const description =
  "kotoba-lang, clj, kami engine, murakumo inference, and LLM integration for a browser-first EDA semiconductor development app.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <main class="md-body kotoba-eda-page">
    <p><a href="/en/">Jun Kawasaki</a> / ADR-2606291100</p>

    <h1>kotoba-lang EDA</h1>
    <p>
      半導体開発を web で完結するための設計。<code>.kotoba</code> / <code>.cljc</code>
      を EDA IR と workflow の正本にし、kami engine で schematic / layout / waveform を描画し、
      murakumo inference と LLM を検証可能な proposal として統合する。
    </p>

    <p>
      <a href="/adr/kotoba-eda-web-semiconductor-app.md">Markdown ADR</a>
      ·
      <a href="/adr/kotoba-eda-web-semiconductor-app.edn">Machine-readable EDN</a>
      ·
      <a href="https://github.com/com-junkawasaki/root/blob/main/90-docs/adr/2606291100-kotoba-eda-web-semiconductor-app.md">Source on GitHub</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Architecture</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Browser IDE:</strong> project, source, canvas, verification, and copilot panes.</li>
      <li><strong>kotoba store:</strong> specs, netlists, layouts, reports, waivers, reviews, and releases as datoms.</li>
      <li><strong>kami engine:</strong> WebGPU schematic graph, physical layout, waveform, timing path, and package views.</li>
      <li><strong>murakumo + LLM:</strong> scale-to-zero CPU/GPU jobs for inference and heavy EDA runs.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Flow</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Spec:</strong> requirements, interfaces, clocks, resets, power domains, and test intent as EDN datoms.</li>
      <li><strong>Design:</strong> <code>.kotoba</code> / <code>.cljc</code> generators for RTL, PCell, constraints, and testbenches.</li>
      <li><strong>Verification:</strong> lint, simulation, formal, DRC, LVS, STA, and SPICE runs normalized to reports.</li>
      <li><strong>Review:</strong> LLM summaries and fix candidates captured as <code>:eda.review/*</code> proposals.</li>
      <li><strong>Release:</strong> sign-off bundle from immutable input/output CIDs, tool versions, reports, and waivers.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Safety Boundary</h2>
    <p>
      EDA reports are authoritative. LLM output is advisory and must become a review datom before it can be accepted.
      PDK licensing, customer NDA, export constraints, external model provider use, paid scale-up, waiver creation,
      and release candidate creation are policy-gated and auditable.
    </p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
